--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Chromium (chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Playwright downloads and bundles a Chromium browser binary into the
published Docker image (`playwright install chromium` in the Dockerfile)
for the stored-login browser feature to drive. Chromium is BSD-licensed
with numerous bundled third-party components under their own licenses; see
Chromium's own credits at chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/LICENSE
rather than reproduced here.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Caddy (github.com/caddyserver/caddy) — used, not bundled
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
The optional VPS deployment path (vps/docker-compose.yml) runs Caddy as a
separate container alongside Anton's, pulled directly from its own
official Docker Hub image (caddy:2.9) to provide HTTPS. Unlike the
entries above, Caddy's binary is never copied into or redistributed as
part of Anton's own image — listed here for transparency about what a VPS
install runs, not because Anton bundles it. Caddy is Apache-2.0 licensed;
see the project's own repository for its full license text.
